---
description: Inventory governing sources, scenario histories and the requested generated behavior.
args:
  request: CompilerRequest
  snapshot: ProcedureSnapshot
returns: Intake
---
1. Inventory snapshot.records by original id and path, retaining text/hash throughout classification.
   Read declared source role and issuer before using organizational folder names as supplementary context.
2. Place adoption, replacement and authority records in editions. Put substantive process descriptions
   in rules, scoped waivers in exceptions, and factual coding/identity/output conventions in context.
3. A mixed record can contribute separately declared clauses to multiple roles, but every later
   interpretation cites the exact original section; repeated classification is not repeated authority.
4. Retain scenario event histories as snapshot.scenarios. Check requested requiredScenarios against
   visible scenario IDs and expose a missing scenario instead of supplying an invented easy example.
5. Call interpretGoal(request, context). Consume required behavior, preserved uncertainty and output
   responsibilities. The compiler cannot change the objective to make its current candidate pass.
6. Keep all historical editions. Edition selection needs to decide which old clauses remain active
   for earlier events and which are replaced only for later events; filename recency cannot decide it.
7. Preserve unclassified records as context with an unresolved ownership finding. Scenario statements
   report actual events, not new normative amendments, even when their actor asserts a permission.
8. Return snapshot, request, goal, editions, rules, exceptions, scenarios, context and unresolved.
   This stage owns source-role and scenario inventory, not validity of any claimed procedure rule.
